# Frontend Rules

## Design System (from docs/DESIGN.md)
- Primary color: #7C3AED (purple only)
- Dark mode bg: #000000, surface: #1C1C1E
- Light mode bg: #F2F2F7, surface: #FFFFFF
- Font: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, SF Pro Text, Arial
- NO rainbow/HSL colors on tags or role badges
- Tags always neutral: rgba(255,255,255,0.06) dark / rgba(0,0,0,0.04) light
- NO colored initials avatars — use Icons.User silhouette on #3A3A3C

## Components
- Use ContactAvatar for all contact photos (handles photo/fallback)
- Use themeStyles object for all colors (not hardcoded)
- Icons are in the Icons object in App.tsx — reuse, never add external icon libraries
- Toast system: use showToast() — never use alert()

## UX Requirements
- Every async action MUST have a loading state
- Every form MUST have an error state
- Empty states MUST have a message + CTA button
- Touch targets minimum 44×44px
- All modals closeable via overlay click or X button

## Prohibited
- No vendor names in UI ("Groq", "Supabase", "Resend", "Expo")
- No bright role badge colors
- No inline `alert()` or `confirm()` — use Toast or modal
- No hardcoded user data in production flows
